# Search parameters for the self-driving `auto-optimize` command — tracked
# in git, like run-config.env. Edit, commit, run `deploy/update.sh` on the droplet, then
# `sudo systemctl start eval-auto-optimize` to kick off a fresh search.
#
# This is NOT `enable`d at boot and NOT auto-restarted on failure or
# completion (see eval-auto-optimize.service) — it's a one-off, bounded
# search you trigger by hand, not an always-on service like eval-harness.
#
# Same flags as `python3 scripts/eval_harness.py auto-optimize` — see
# eval/README.md. MUST stay double-quoted — see run-config.env's comment
# for why (this file is bash-`source`d too, not systemd's EnvironmentFile
# format).
#
# --baseline-run is deliberately OMITTED below — eval_harness.py resolves it
# itself when not given (_resolve_default_baseline_run(): the run that
# tested the live current prompt version), and that's the ONE place this
# resolution logic lives, used by every invocation path alike (this systemd
# unit via auto_optimize.sh, the web dashboard's "Launch more rounds", and
# a bare CLI call). Real incident this was built to fix: this file used to
# carry a static --baseline-run value that went 80+ versions stale, silently
# — nothing here re-derives "what's actually current," and a hardcoded
# value can only ever drift further behind, never self-correct. Do NOT add
# --baseline-run back to this file as a static value for that reason — if
# you need to pin a specific baseline for one deliberate run, pass
# --baseline-run on the command line for that invocation only, or use the
# dashboard's "Use as baseline" button, rather than committing a value here
# that every future run silently inherits.
AUTO_OPTIMIZE_ARGS="--rounds 5 --concurrency 6 --time-budget-minutes 60"
